    "body": "## Summary\n- expose the existing backend final checkpoint as `Potwierdź dotarcie do punktu B`\n- keep A, intermediate-stop and B confirmation behind the same server-side fresh-GPS/proximity guard\n- recognize `ARRIVED_DESTINATION` as a terminal route phase in the web UI\n- stop the browser geolocation watcher immediately after final arrival\n- hide live ETA/stale/awaiting-GPS messaging once the route has arrived at B\n- show an explicit completed-route state explaining that precise GPS and ETA were cleared by the backend\n- keep route arrival separate from job completion and settlement, with a direct link back to job details for `Zgłoś wykonanie`\n- make the terminal tracking phase monotonic in client state so stale polling/realtime/GPS responses cannot visually roll the route back after B was confirmed\n- document the final destination web behavior and privacy boundary\n\n## Privacy\nAfter `ARRIVED_DESTINATION`, the browser stops requesting GPS updates and the UI no longer displays a courier marker or ETA. The backend remains authoritative and already clears the latest precise position at final arrival. No location history is introduced.\n\n## Lifecycle\nConfirming B only ends route tracking. It does not mark the job DONE, confirm completion, release escrow, or otherwise alter payment settlement. Those actions remain on the normal job lifecycle.\n\n## Validation\nRun production dependency audit, ESLint, Vite build, backend Maven verify and the full runtime smoke. Do not merge unless the latest head is green.",
